@@ -0,0 +1,20 @@
+---
+kind: upgrade-guide
+description: "Buildr plugin installation and updates require uninstalling the existing Buildr bundle first."
+---
+
+# Buildr plugin installations are mutually exclusive
+
+English | [中文](guide.zh.md)
+
+## Change
+
+Profiles previously accepted separate Buildr release and development packages, and pnpm could update the same package in place. The install form and shared installer now refuse a Buildr install when a Buildr bundle is already installed, even when disabled or installed through a direct npm alias. The refusal identifies the existing package and asks the user to uninstall it first; it neither switches versions nor deletes configuration or sessions. An unidentifiable source fails its identity check when a Buildr bundle is installed. Identified unrelated packages continue normally.
+
+## Migration
+
+1. Read the existing Buildr package name in the Plugins page. Disabling it does not satisfy the installation check.
+2. Complete that package's supported withdrawal before uninstalling it. If preset rows reference files inside a development composition, restore those references and the original DSH modules before removing its package; this installation check does not automate withdrawal.
+3. Install the selected Buildr version. Confirm that it is the only installed Buildr bundle and that installing another version reports the existing package and asks for uninstallation.
+
+The [plugin manager reference](../../../../packages/boot/plugin-manager/README.md) defines the recognized packages and identification limits. These actions require a DSH runtime containing the new installer; compiling a Buildr plugin or an SDK alone does not update an installed desktop application.
